# Manuals are binary, and git does not always work that out for itself. The Level 2 Sixel
# Programming Reference staged as 5909 lines of TEXT rather than as a blob, which means Windows
# line-ending conversion would have rewritten bytes inside the PDF and produced a file that no
# reader could open - from a clone that looked clean.
*.pdf binary

# Conformance corpora are DATA, not source. Their bytes are the test.
#
# Git on Windows would otherwise turn every LF into CRLF on checkout, which changes the
# streams being fed to the emulator and the expected screens being compared against. A
# fresh clone would then disagree with this machine for a reason nobody could see in a
# diff - the files would look identical.
#
# -text means "never convert line endings in either direction".
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/xtermjs/*.in    -text
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/xtermjs/*.text  -text
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/xtermjs/NOTES   -text
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/libvterm/*.test -text
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/tektronix/**    -text
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/vt340test/**    -text
